<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#rice">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Rice</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Rice is a cereal grain cultivated in flooded paddies or dry fields and is a staple food across much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia">Asia</a> and parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a>. It underpinned the economies of many empires, including the Han, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a> and Ming dynasties of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khmer-empire">Khmer</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit</a> empires of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/southeast-asia">Southeast Asia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa Shogunate</a>, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samurai">samurai</a> stipends were measured in rice. It also appears in the profiles of the Mughal and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> empires in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, the Sasanian and Safavid empires in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songhai-empire">Songhai</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaabu-empire">Kaabu</a> empires in West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>.</p></div>
